## 6. Acceptance Criteria

P4-02 is PASS only when:

### Co-Guardian security
- Invitation specifies explicit selected Student IDs.
- Invitation creator must have active access to each selected Student.
- Claim creates links only for selected Students.
- No blanket workspace-wide child linking occurs.
- Existing Guardians and links remain intact.
- Cross-Guardian access tests pass.

### Family curriculum
- Admin can create and publish a Family program.
- Program versions are immutable after publication.
- Program items reference exact published content versions.
- Program ordering is stable.
- Existing enrolled Students retain their pinned version after a newer version is published.

### Teacher-free learning
- Family-only Student can receive an activated program.
- No Teacher is required.
- No School Organization or Class is required.
- Student can login independently.
- Student can start and resume learning.
- Turns persist.
- Retry, completion and abandonment work correctly.
- Existing P2-06 semantics are preserved.

### Cross-context identity
- A Student with School and Family contexts retains one canonical user identity.
- School memberships remain unchanged.
- Existing assignments remain usable.
- Family learning does not create duplicate Student users.
- Guardian linking does not create duplicate Student users.

### Guardian progress
- Guardian sees only explicitly linked Students.
- Guardian sees only descriptive program/Chapter statuses.
- Guardian cannot retrieve raw attempt or turn data.
- Guardian cannot retrieve emotion, Body Map, intensity, strategy or AAC choices.
- Guardian cannot retrieve Teacher observations.
- Guardian cannot retrieve another Guardian's exclusively linked Student.
- Guardian dashboard never describes completion as mastery or SEL improvement.

### Privacy
- No unauthorized workspace or Student access.
- Revoked relationships stop access.
- Invitation codes remain hashed and single-use.
- No sensitive content in logs or error messages.
- No private data leakage in API DTOs.

### Regression and build
- TypeScript passes.
- Production build passes.
- All P1–P4-01 automated tests remain passing.
- New P4-02 tests pass.
- Existing School and Teacher flows remain intact.
- Health endpoints remain healthy.
- No database migration is executed.
- No live TiDB writes occur.

Clearly report PASS, FAIL and NOT RUN.

Mock tests must not be presented as live DB or browser verification.

